{"key":"apphy2-mcq-006","kind":"mcq","model":"google/gemini-3.8-flash","pass":"solve","ok":true,"object":{"chosen_label":"A","final_answer":"zero","working":"Let the two identical positive charges, each with charge +q, be located at positions -d and +d along a horizontal line. The midpoint is at position 0. The electric field produced by the left charge at the midpoint points away from it (to the right) with magnitude E = kq/d^2. The electric field produced by the right charge at the midpoint points away from it (to the left) with the same magnitude E = kq/d^2. By the principle of superposition, the two electric field vectors have equal magnitudes and opposite directions, so they cancel completely, resulting in a net electric field of zero.","defect":""},"usage":{"inputTokens":360,"inputTokenDetails":{"noCacheTokens":360,"cacheReadTokens":0},"outputTokens":415,"outputTokenDetails":{"textTokens":164,"reasoningTokens":251},"totalTokens":775,"raw":{"thoughtsTokenCount":251,"promptTokenCount":360,"candidatesTokenCount":164,"totalTokenCount":775,"trafficType":"ON_DEMAND","promptTokensDetails":[{"modality":"TEXT","tokenCount":360}],"candidatesTokensDetails":[{"modality":"TEXT","tokenCount":164}]},"reasoningTokens":251,"cachedInputTokens":0},"attempts":1,"mode":"object","ms":125982,"keyed_label":"A"}
